cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "eVTOL Conceptual Sizing Tool"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Vinay Kumar Reddy"
    family-names: "Sirigireddy"
    email: "sirigireddy.vinaykumarreddy@wright.edu"
    affiliation: "Wright State University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vinay25112001/eVTOLSizer"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based conceptual sizing tool for electric VTOL aircraft, built on
  NDARC/AFDD weight models. It sizes six configurations (multicopter,
  side-by-side, lift+cruise, tiltrotor and two hybrid layouts) and is validated
  against the published weight statements of NASA's UAM concept vehicles
  (NASA/TM-20210017971 Table 12) and against manufacturer figures for
  commercial types. Group errors are reported against AFDD's own published
  in-population accuracy (NDARC Theory Manual Table 27-21) rather than a
  self-chosen tolerance. Credibility is self-assessed against NASA-STD-7009B;
  the generated VALIDATION.md carries the current numbers and the assessment,
  including the factors scored zero.
keywords:
  - eVTOL
  - conceptual design
  - aircraft sizing
  - NDARC
  - rotorcraft
  - urban air mobility
  - verification and validation
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
